e current board state.\n            epsilon: float or None. Exploration rate. If None, uses self.epsilon.\n            \n        Returns:\n            int: Action index in [0, 8].\n        \"\"\"\n        ...\n    def learn(self, obs: np.ndarray, action: int, reward: float, next_obs: np.ndarray, terminated: bool) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Update the Q-value for the observed transition.\n        \n        Args:\n            obs: np.ndarray of shape (9,), the state before the action.\n            action: int, the action taken.\n            reward: float, the reward received.\n            next_obs: np.ndarray of shape (9,), the state after the action.\n            terminated: bool, True if the episode ended (terminal state).\n        \"\"\"\n        ...\nclass RandomAgent:\n    \"\"\"A baseline agent that selects valid actions uniformly at random.\n    \n    Note: It does not check legal actions internally; it assumes the environment\n    or caller provides valid actions. This is suitable for testing in Tic-Tac-Toe\n    where any unoccupied cell is valid.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def get_action(self, obs: np.ndarray) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Select a random action index in [0, 8].\n        \n        Args:\n            obs: np.ndarray of shape (9,), the current board state.\n            \n        Returns:\n            int: A random action index in [0, 8].\n        \"\"\"\n        ...\nclass StaticAgent:\n    \"\"\"An optimal static agent for Tic-Tac-Toe.\n    \n    Implements a perfect strategy using minimax logic. It never loses and wins\n    if the opponent makes a mistake.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def get_action(self, obs: np.ndarray) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Get the optimal move for the current player.\n        \n        Args:\n            obs: np.ndarray of shape (9,), the current board state.\n            \n        Returns:\n            int: The best action index in [0, 8].\n        \"\"\"\n        ...",
